---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Sarh Al Elm Private School" lang="en">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">About Us</p><h1>A community built on strong foundations</h1><p class="sub">Established in 2004, Sarh Al Elm serves learners from Kindergarten 1 and 2 through Grade 8 in Muscat.</p></div></section>
  <section class="block wrap two-col"><div><h2>Our story</h2><p>Established in 2004, Sarh Al Elm Private School has served families in South Al Mawaleh for more than two decades. The school welcomes Omani and expatriate learners from Kindergarten 1 and 2 through Grade 8.</p><p>Our name — meaning “the edifice of knowledge” — reflects the idea that learning is built step by step. We aim to provide a purposeful bilingual school experience in which students build knowledge, communication skills, confidence and positive learning habits.</p><h2 class="mt">Our educational approach</h2><p>We seek to keep pace with developments in education through modern teaching strategies, educational resources and interactive learning technologies. Our approach supports the wider goals of Oman Vision 2040 by valuing education, innovation, capable people and sustainable national development.</p></div><div><h2>Our vision</h2><p>Together for sustainable development through forward-looking, technology-enabled thinking and effective community partnership.</p><h2 class="mt">Our mission</h2><p>We seek to provide high-quality educational services supported by sustainable technology, equipping students with knowledge, skills and values through creative educators who use modern teaching approaches and engage the wider community to meet present and future challenges.</p><h2 class="mt">Our values</h2><p>We promote Islamic and humanitarian values, integrity, respect, responsibility, continuous learning, innovation and meaningful community participation, while giving students attentive academic and personal support.</p><h2 class="mt">Curriculum information</h2><p>Sarh Al Elm teaches the Oman Ministry of Education Mathematics and Science curriculum and learning resources developed through the Ministry’s partnership with Cambridge University Press & Assessment.</p><a class="text-link" href="/academics/">Explore academics →</a></div></section>

  <section class="why"><div class="wrap"><div class="why-head"><p class="eyebrow">Why Sarh Al Elm?</p><h2>Purposeful learning, supportive guidance and a balanced school experience</h2><p>The Sarh Al Elm experience brings together learning, values, care and opportunities that help students grow with confidence.</p></div><div class="why-grid">
    <article><span class="why-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><h3>Quality Education</h3><p>We aim to provide purposeful learning that combines academic knowledge with skills students can carry into everyday life and future learning.</p></article>
    <article><span class="why-icon" aria-hidden="true">◎</span><h3>Experienced Teachers</h3><p>The school draws on educational experience across different disciplines and stages, with an emphasis on clear and engaging teaching.</p></article>
    <article><span class="why-icon" aria-hidden="true">◇</span><h3>Supportive Learning Environment</h3><p>We seek to provide a safe and encouraging school environment where students can learn, build confidence and develop in a balanced way.</p></article>
    <article><span class="why-icon" aria-hidden="true">♡</span><h3>Student Support & Guidance</h3><p>We value ongoing follow-up and support for students as they grow academically and personally.</p></article>
    <article><span class="why-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><h3>Values & Integrity</h3><p>Islamic and humanitarian values, respect and responsibility are encouraged as important parts of students’ character development.</p></article>
    <article><span class="why-icon" aria-hidden="true">☆</span><h3>Enriching Activities</h3><p>Cultural, sporting, artistic and community activities help students explore their talents, participate and develop their personalities.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.page-hero{position:relative;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(4,34,62,.92),rgba(4,34,62,.62)),url('/images/school/03-school-celebration.jpg') center 60%/cover;color:#fff;padding:92px 0}.page-hero .eyebrow{color:#d5a43f;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:12px}.page-hero h1{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:14px;max-width:640px}.page-hero .sub{color:#eef5fb;max-width:560px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7}.block{padding:64px 24px}.two-col{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:48px}h2{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--navy-dark)}h2.mt{margin-top:28px}p{color:var(--ink);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px}.text-link{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none}@media(max-width:800px){.page-hero{padding:70px 0;background-position:center}.two-col{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.why{background:#f4f7f9;padding:78px 0}.why-head{text-align:center;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 38px}.why-head .eyebrow{color:var(--gold);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}.why-head h2{font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);margin:8px 0 12px}.why-head>p:last-child{color:var(--slate)}.why-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}.why-grid article{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3e9ee;border-radius:14px;padding:30px 26px;text-align:center;box-shadow:0 5px 18px rgba(14,42,70,.035)}.why-icon{display:grid;place-items:center;width:52px;height:52px;margin:0 auto 18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;font-size:23px;transition:transform .3s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1),background .3s ease}.why-grid article:hover .why-icon{transform:translateY(-3px) scale(1.08);background:#176a91}.why-grid h3{color:var(--navy-dark);font-size:18px;margin-bottom:9px}.why-grid p{color:var(--slate);font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;margin:0}@media(max-width:800px){.why{padding:58px 0}.why-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:540px){.why-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.why-icon{transition:none!important;transform:none!important}}</style>